    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "CITYWIDE present 58 Broombridge Road, an exciting opportunity to purchase beautifully presented home, benefitting from off-street carparking to the front and a long west-facing rear garden.\nThis turn-key property consists of an entrance hallway, an open plan living / dining / kitchen area at ground floor level. At first floor level there are two double bedrooms and a shower room.\n\nLocated in the Cabra area of Dublin 7, the location is an established residential setting, with excellent accessibility to the city. This accessibility will be further enhanced with both the Broombridge LUAS and Train Stations just at the end of the road. Another new Train Station located in the neighbouring Hamilton Gardens development on Carnlough Road, which is currently in the planning process. As part of the DART expansion plan, this Cabra Station will connect with the existing Phoenix Park Tunnel line and connect with Connolly & Grand Canal Dock.\n\nACCOMMODATION\nThis 1940`s constructed mid-terrace home has ample off-street carparking to the front, ideal for electric car charging.\nInside, the hallway leads us to bright and spacious open plan living / dining / kitchen, with wood laminate floors continuing through from the hallway and giving a flow between the spaces. \nThis open plan space has an enviable dual aspect layout with glazing on both the east and west sides of the home, creating a bright and airy feel throughout the day.\nThe space could suit a variety of different layouts, with the current layout of the living space to the front feeling cosy, while the dining space to the rear has the benefit of glazed double doors leading the long west-facing rear garden.\nTo the side of the space, the kitchen area is both stylish and practical, with an abundance of storage space and countertop space. A white tiled splashback contrasts with darker countertops., and integrated downlighting give a sleek finish to the kitchen space.\n\nAt first floor level, the primary bedroom is to the front, with fitted wardrobes cleverly added to both sides of the room. The second bedroom is to the rear, while slightly smaller than the primary bedroom, it`s another good sized double bedroom, and is a versatile room that could suit a variety of different uses.\nThe shower room is another stylishly presented space, with a modern suite and an electric shower fitted. The bathroom is fully tiled and has the benefit of both an external window and electric ventilation.\nAll glazing throughout the house is double glazed, gas-fired central heating and a modern external insulation has been fitted to the front and rear of the property.\n\nGARDEN\nThe long back garden has the ideal west-facing orientation, meaning the space will get maximum sunlight in afternoons and evenings, ideal for summer barbeques.\nGiven the exceptional length of the garden, there is excellent potential to extend the house to the rear and / or add a garden room, while still retaining a great size garden.\n\n\nFLOOR AREAS\nGROUND FLOOR\nHallway 2.86m x 1.77m\nOpen Plan Space\nLiving Area 3.73m x 2.99m\nDining Area 2.53m x 2.99m\nKitchen 3.40m x 1.77m\n\nFIRST FLOOR\nPrimary Bedroom 3.30m x 3.98m\nBedroom Two 2.78m x 3.36m\nShower Room 1.74m x 1.56m\n+Landing\n\nTOTAL FLOOR AREA 61m2 / 657 sq ft\n\n\nLOCATION\nBroombridge Road is a mature residential setting in Cabra, and in close proximity to Royal Canal Park, Stoneybatter, Phibsborough, Smithfield and the north city centre, and an easy cycle commute across the city.\nThe area benefits from a variety of public transport links (LUAS Crosscity Broombridge Stop and Train Station, various Dublin Bus Routes and a new train line and station being developed at the neighbouring Hamilton Gardens development on Carnlough Road), and has good accessibility to N3 towards Blanchardstown, and M50 / Airport via the adjoining Navan Road.\nThe property is in close proximity to numerous local amenities with a variety of retail options and creches in the neighbouring Hamilton Gardens development and Royal Canal Park development just a 5min walk away. Further retail and dining options are a further 10mins away on the Cabra Road, leading to the bustling centre of Phibsborough and the adjoining DIT / TU Dublin Grangegorman Campus.\n\nVIEWING IS HIGHLY RECOMMENDED & VIA CITYWIDE\n\n(These particulars do not constitute an offer or contract, and whilst every effort has been made in preparing all descriptions, dimensions, maps, and plans, these details should not be relied upon as fact. Dimensions / Illustrations are for guideline purposes only and not to scale. CITYWIDE will not hold itself responsible for any inaccuracies contained therein.)\n"
      },
